"""Export an explicitly exploratory appendix draft from saved summary metrics."""
import argparse
import json
from pathlib import Path

def render(out,dest):
    p=out/'metrics.json';metrics=json.loads(p.read_text()) if p.exists() else {}
    plan=json.loads((out/'analysis_plan.json').read_text())
    ready=bool(metrics);complete=bool(plan.get('complete'))
    lines=['# Exploratory appendix candidate: token-stream monitoring','',
      '**Author decision required for inclusion.** This is a separate post hoc analysis; it does not replace the frozen main results. '+('The full horizon sweep is complete.' if complete else 'The full horizon sweep and expanded blocking-point analysis are not yet complete.'),'',
      '## Candidate paragraph','',
      'In an exploratory follow-up, we asked whether a probe can recognize a leaking reply while the target is producing its reasoning. We reused the frozen family-grouped folds and held-out-scenario rotations, adding each episode’s first public-emission request to the strictly pre-emission cohort. The resulting cohort contains 2,205 replies from 238 recruiting episodes; 1,995 replies have saved reasoning, including 121 of 146 first-emission replies. We fitted reply-weighted linear probes separately for emission in the current reply, within one, two, or three subsequent eligible replies, and the paper’s round-based near-term label. Each reply was scored by its maximum or mean token score. The frozen last-prompt near-term probe was evaluated on identical replies, but its channel-outcome training label differs from the any-public-emission reply-horizon labels. We also removed reasoning from the first exact-value mention onward and compared with fixed keyword and observed-prefix-count baselines. These analyses test offline discrimination and possible warning opportunities, not a deployed prevention system.','',
      'The broader blocking-point experiment follows streaming-probe ideas in Constitutional Classifiers++ [@cunningham2026, §5.1], with separately ablated 16-token logit smoothing and softmax-weighted losses. It uses four fixed full layers or independent 256-dimensional projections of each of 24 layers, rather than full all-layer features. Its EMA coefficient of 2/17 is our choice. A uniform max-of-rolling-means comparison is motivated by the probe literature discussed by Kramár et al. [@kramar2026, §3.2.2]; that paper attributes the uniform method to McKenzie et al. [@mckenzie2026], and adds attention weighting that we do not reproduce. First-flag truncation follows the evaluation idea in Constitutional Classifiers [@sharma2025constitutional, Appendix A.4]. Thresholds use other-fold control-reply maxima at a nominal 5% false-alarm rate; this is not a 5% episode-level guarantee. Family-bootstrap intervals condition on fitted models and selected layers.','',
      '## Candidate results table','',
      '| Label | Cut | Split | Replies / positives | Reasoning MAX AUROC [95% CI] | Reasoning mean | Frozen last-prompt A |',
      '|---|---|---|---:|---|---|---|']
    def fmt(r):
        if not r or 'within_round_auc' not in r:return 'Pending'
        lo,hi=r['within_round_ci95'];return f"{r['within_round_auc']:.3f} [{lo:.3f}, {hi:.3f}]"
    for variant in ['immediate','h1','h2','h3','round']:
      for mask in ['all','censored']:
       for mode in ['pooled','loso']:
        key=f'{variant}/{mask}/{mode}/extended/'
        r=metrics.get(key+'token_max',{})
        count=f"{r['rows']} / {r['positives']}" if r else 'Pending'
        lines.append(f"| {variant} | {mask} | {mode} | {count} | {fmt(r)} | {fmt(metrics.get(key+'token_mean'))} | {fmt(metrics.get(key+'frozen_last_prompt_A'))} |")
    lines += ['','CIs are family-bootstrap 95% intervals; AUROC compares replies within scenario × round. The table must not be presented as a pure activation-position comparison because the frozen comparator has a different training label for k=0–3. Keyword, combined-stream and expanded-capture results belong alongside this table once their separate checks finish.','',
      '## Candidate main-text pointer','',
      'An exploratory appendix examines whether token-stream probes can identify an imminent disclosure within the reply, using frozen family splits, matched text baselines, and explicit pre-disclosure cutoffs.','',
      '## Editorial provenance (not manuscript prose)','',
      f'Source: `{out}/metrics.json`, generated by `experiments/E05-probes/reasoning_stream_appendix.py`; no hand-entered performance numbers. Full scripts, source hashes, run folders, costs, keyword specification, and deviations are listed in the source report’s Provenance and citations section. Expanded replay cost remains pending shutdown reconciliation. McKenzie key mckenzie2026 was supplied by the bibliography owner from the arXiv BibTeX export; its verified entry was committed in 27d2d576. Source: https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10805. The other three citation keys were checked against report/references.bib.']
    for comparison in sorted(out.glob('comparison-*.json')):
        record=json.loads(comparison.read_text())
        lines+=['','## Immediate-reply text comparison','','Six sampled text prefixes versus every saved reasoning token; different sampling may affect both timing and MAX ranking.','', '| Cut | Split | Method | Stratified AUROC [95% CI] | Warning | Held alarms |','|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|']
        for r in record['records']:
            lo,hi=r['ci95'];rate=lambda x:'Not evaluated' if x is None else f'{x:.1%}'
            lines.append(f"| {r['cut']} | {r['split']} | {r['method']} | {r['within_auc']:.3f} [{lo:.3f}, {hi:.3f}] | {rate(r['warning'])} | {rate(r['held_alarm'])} |")
    dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);dest.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')

if __name__=='__main__':
 p=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--out',type=Path,required=True);p.add_argument('--dest',type=Path,default=Path('report/appendix_drafts/streaming_exploratory.md'));a=p.parse_args();render(a.out,a.dest)
